# Conditional lifetime event ledger

`ledger.py` implements a typed metadata ledger for a finite classical sequence of
atomic requests and coherent external lookup calls. It does not execute an
adaptive quantum driver. It sums reviewed component costs and constructs an
explicit disjoint logical-register allocation for the selected sequence.
All complete-resource, primitive-bridge, physical-workspace and qualification
flags remain false. No production gate or captured machine source is changed.

The source boundary consists of the exact accepted observation
`81ffb1db693c94f73f41239da3cd8164893d9c84ddd805d873ec3ede974f4f4c`, its
38 source and30 implementation pins, and the three additional family, dispatcher
and L0 identities. The observation is read once, and those exact bytes are hashed
before JSON parsing. All72 paths are checked before and after accounting.
This authenticates selected identities; it does not establish a complete Python
or compiler dependency closure, or replace the component correctness premises.
The Python host and this checker are trusted.

## Supported cases

| Event | Boundary | Derived resource vector |
|---|---|---|
| Accepted REG | Either row; body4096 bytes, six256-byte contexts, list0 | Captured generator and return, analytically rebased W |
| Accepted VOTE | Either row; body0, six empty contexts, list1000; valid content is a premise | Same; accepted-only97+proof result |
| Size-rejected VOTE | Either row, fixed actual u64 length outside3..1000 | Source-bound header and253+proof result; full typed list storage retained |
| External lookup | Source-padded same F, supplied full message capacity | Exact L0 scan formula; two base calls, including disabled queries |

Other accepted lengths and the bounded-content P0/ContentFamily resource vectors
are refused. Those circuits exist, but these four observations do not price all
of them. This ledger does not infer a family maximum or silently use their wider
return envelope. Request lengths and role/row descriptors are caller metadata;
authentication against a real request is an external obligation.

Every event must carry the same `Interface(N,b,oracle,completion)`, where
`N=T*(2^20+2)` and b>=23 also accommodates the current maximum honest query.
The oracle and completion strings are equality tokens supplied by the caller,
not certificates of a physical oracle. Requests include size rejection in T.
Queries have an independently bounded count Q and full message capacity C with
6882996<=C<2^b. The source-padded response is2112 bits. Neither query count nor
stored-key width implies a full-query length bound.

## Accounting and ownership

At a different T/b, the accepted observation's generator and E costs stay fixed.
The source-derived W formula is re-evaluated, including the counter width
`d=max(2,N.bit_length())`, complete staging, fixed M+2 scans, log bits, append
scratch and maximum shared scratch. At T=2^44,b=64 the tool reproduces all four
original full gate vectors and total logical-register sizes exactly. This is a
checked analytical rebase, not a new execution of their full elementary streams.

Known body costs are summed as (X,CX,CCX,F), with elementary subtotal X+CX+5CCX.
Retained private coin count is subtracted from original input count exactly once
to obtain public input count. One log/counter is allocated for the whole trace.
All request inputs/coins/outputs and query/enable/response slots are distinct and
retained. Only the clean boundary workspace is shared, at the maximum of each
request's retained-derived plus shared work and each lookup's work. Optional
explicit placements must have the exact required sizes and disjoint intervals.
These placements are a logical ownership map; no circuit relocation is executed.

Each accepted event reserves M+2 slots, including the possible exhausted schedule;
size rejection reserves zero. The prefix reservation proves conservative capacity
for the selected metadata trace. Actual counter values, accepted trial counts,
written values and occupancy are not computed or inferred from that reservation.
Duplicate key bytes are permitted; aliasing register allocations is not.

The classical-retained model assumes supplied fresh uniformly mixed coin registers
and keeps them allocated. It gives no free disposal/reset or entropy preparation.
The purified-retained model also allocates each purifier and reports separately
R Hadamards plus R CNOTs for the canonical preparation from2R zero wires. This
preparation is not run or folded into the body subtotal. Both models need freshness
independent of the entering history, not independence conditioned on the completed
adaptive trace.

Entire quantum support must satisfy canonical query and active-record encodings.
An agreed total F completion does not enforce this condition. The same immutable F
and log contracts must hold jointly with adversary/reference state; honest requests
remain classical and atomic, with no interleaving inside compute/write/return/
uncompute or between L0's two base calls. Arbitrary correlations on disjoint
registers are allowed by the component contract; no quantum cloning is supplied.

Unknown terms remain explicit: adversary gates/storage, initial state and entropy,
input/descriptor preparation, adaptive selection, routing, base-oracle implementation
and state, uniform bounds over all allowed traces/families, and the primitive entry
bridge/advantages. The allocated known bits are not full experiment memory, physical
qubits, native allocation, or the64MiB verification workspace.

## Commands and refusal

From the repository root, with all outputs restricted to this ignored stage:

```sh
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 PYTEST_ADDOPTS='' PYTEST_PLUGINS='' /opt/homebrew/bin/pytest -q --noconftest -p no:cacheprovider target/parliament-lifetime-composition-stage/test_ledger.py --basetemp target/parliament-lifetime-composition-stage/test-temp --maxfail=0
python3 -B target/parliament-lifetime-composition-stage/ledger.py --root . --events target/parliament-lifetime-composition-stage/example.json
```

`--require-qualified` emits the identical conditional report and exits2. Bad
metadata, unsupported cases, source drift or ownership conflicts exit1 without a
report. A successful ordinary exit0 means only that this conditional ledger's
checks passed. The retained receipt records exact commands and outcomes after local review;
it cannot turn the conditional premises into independent cryptographic review.

